{
  /*
   * There was no tsconfig.json in this project until 2026-08-04, which is why
   * `npm run check` had never run and no .astro file had ever been type-checked
   * (R-03). `astro check` needs one, plus @astrojs/check and typescript, both of
   * which were added to devDependencies with this file.
   *
   * The preset is Astro's own `strict`, unchanged. It is what `astro add` writes
   * for a new project, so it is the setting a reader can check against the
   * upstream default rather than against a judgement made here — and this repo
   * already forbids `any`, so the weaker `base` preset would have been a
   * standard set below the one the code is written to.
   *
   * `strictest` was NOT chosen. It turns on noUncheckedIndexedAccess and
   * exactOptionalPropertyTypes, which change what correct code has to look like
   * rather than what it has to mean. Raising to it is a decision for whoever is
   * prepared to do the refactor, not a side effect of turning type-checking on
   * for the first time.
   *
   * Nothing here is loosened to make the check pass. If it fails, it has found
   * something.
   */
  "extends": "astro/tsconfigs/strict",
  "include": [".astro/types.d.ts", "**/*"],
  "exclude": ["dist", "node_modules"]
}
